   PD (5,3,1,0), c = P = 1, exact: section of a commitment p and its guarantee
      p = 0: q in [0, 0], inf u_1 = u_1(p, 0) = 1, u_2 there = 1
      p = 1/4: q in [1/15, 4/5], inf u_1 = u_1(p, 1/15) = 1, u_2 there = 23/12
      p = 1/2: q in [1/7, 1], inf u_1 = u_1(p, 1/7) = 1, u_2 there = 39/14
      p = 1: q in [1/3, 1], inf u_1 = u_1(p, 1/3) = 1, u_2 there = 13/3
      so E(1) = {u >= (1, 1)}, which contains mutual defection (p = q = 0), is a fixed point

